 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>“JAMES, by the grace of God, King of England, Scotland, France and Ireland, Defender of the Faith, etc. . . .</p>\n<p>Our loving Subjects, have been humble Suitors unto us, that We would vouchsafe unto them our Licence, to make Habitation, Plantation, and to deduce a colony of sundry of our People into that part of America commonly called VIRGINIA. . . .</p>\n<p>We, greatly commending, and graciously accepting of, their Desires for the Furtherance of so noble a Work, which may, by the Providence of Almighty God, hereafter tend to the Glory of his Divine Majesty, in propagating of Christian Religion to such People, as yet live in Darkness and miserable Ignorance of the true Knowledge and Worship of God, and may in time bring the Infidels and Savages, living in those parts, to human Civility, and to a settled and quiet Government: DO, by these our Letters Patents, graciously accept of, and agree to, their humble and well-intended Desires.”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">The First Charter of Virginia, April 10, 1606</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided</i>.</p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 614764,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A historian would use the excerpt provided to support which of the following arguments?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167030,
     "content_html": "The English had a predominantly religious motive in establishing the Virginia colony."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167029,
     "content_html": "The Virginia Company was established in an equal partnership with the English monarch."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167028,
     "content_html": "The Spanish incursions in the Chesapeake region influenced the founding of the Virginia colony."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167027,
     "content_html": "The monarch had ultimate control of the business transactions of the Virginia colony."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 614765,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The main motivation for English individuals to travel to Virginia in the early seventeenth-century was to",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167033,
     "content_html": "convert American Indians to Christianity"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167034,
     "content_html": "gain personal wealth"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167032,
     "content_html": "avoid a long sentence in debtors’ prison"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167031,
     "content_html": "fight Spanish pirates"
    }
   ],
